    description: "Observed in session_retrospective_04172026_1012.md Finding 2, and in prior retros 04-09 and 04-14 (3rd consecutive). Selector LLM picks permanently-relevant playbooks (output-capture 47 selections, smart-test 45, recover-state 38, tracker-reply 35, trackerize 35) that are then dedup-filtered before reaching the agent. This session: 244 polls, 466 selections, 72 injections, 394 dedup-skipped = 84.5% waste rate.\n\nProposed improvement: pass the current dedup window (the list of playbook IDs already in the recent context) into the selector prompt as an explicit 'do not re-pick these' precondition. The selector can then spend tokens on genuinely novel candidates instead of re-nominating oscillators. Alternative: demote permanently-relevant playbooks to 'pin once per session' status.\n\nTouches .agent/hooks/_shared/on_transcript_change.py -> needs_human_review per governance rule."  # 991c
